  "conditions": {
    "dedicated": true,
    "detail": "Only this llama-server was resident on the GPU; the image server that normally runs on the box was stopped before the model was loaded, and nvidia-smi listed no other compute process. The only other running container was a small host metrics exporter (python, about 10 MB, no GPU).",
    "isolation_check": "nvidia-smi compute apps -> 3676821, /home/bakeer/llama.cpp-tinfield/build/bin/llama-server ; docker ps -> 1 containers; load1 at start 1.00"
  },
  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Prompt caching is turned off per request (cache_prompt false) on this row. The haystack documents repeat across the prefill and long-context workloads, and with llama-server prompt caching left on an earlier pass of this run measured mostly cache hits: prefill-8k reported a p50 TTFT of 125 ms and 3,113 tok/s against about 960 tok/s cold."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "This llama.cpp build has no --no-mmap flag any more. The equivalent is --load-mode none, which reads the whole GGUF into memory. There is also a new --lazy-mode (default auto) that serves tensors larger than 4 GiB, here the 26.8 GiB engram table, from a memory map on demand; it only applies when the file is memory-mapped. On this box load mode and thread count made no measurable difference to speed (llama-bench tg128 32.0 tok/s and pp2048 1,095 tok/s with load-mode none or auto, 10 or 20 threads), so none was used for a fully resident, repeatable run."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "KV cache is f16. Only 12 of the 48 layers are full attention, so four 131072-token slots of f16 KV fit comfortably. q8_0 K and V were measured as well and were slower at depth: llama-bench tg128 at 32768 tokens of context 23.9 tok/s with q8_0 against 25.6 with f16, prefill equal within noise. The model card suggests -ctk q8_0 -ctv q4_0 to fit 64 GB machines, which is not needed here."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The chat template defaults to reasoning_effort xhigh when thinking is on (accepted values xhigh, medium, low; pass it through chat_template_kwargs). Thinking is parsed into reasoning_content and the answer into content with --jinja; tool calls come back as OpenAI tool_calls with finish_reason tool_calls."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=1 was set for every load, as is usual for large models on GB10 where CUDA VMM allocation can stall the load. A load without it was not tried on this build."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "-np 4 splits -c 524288 into four slots of 131072. -c is the total across slots, so -np 4 -c 131072 would have given each slot 32768 tokens and silently truncated the long-context rows."
    }
  ],
